<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Central Asia and the Steppe</p><h1 class="st-title">Ural Cossack Host</h1><p class="st-meta">1591 CE – 1920 CE (approx.) · capital Uralsk</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A self-governing Cossack community on the Ural River, guardians of Russia's steppe frontier and the starting point of Pugachev's great rebellion.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossacks</a>, many from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/don-river">Don</a>, settled on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ural-river">Yaik</a> River, later renamed the Ural, in the late 16th century, establishing a fishing and raiding community. In 1591 they took part in a Russian campaign, and the host is traditionally dated to that year. Their main town, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oral-kazakhstan">Yaitsky Gorodok</a>, later became Uralsk.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The host was governed by an elected ataman and an assembly, the krug, and lived by fishing for sturgeon and caviar on the river, held in common, and by military service. Many were <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-believers">Old Believers</a>. As the Russian state tightened control, discontent grew; in 1772 a revolt broke out, and in 1773 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ural-river">Yaik</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossacks</a> backed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemelyan-pugachev">Yemelyan Pugachev's</a> rebellion against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catherine-the-great">Catherine the Great</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the revolt, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catherine-the-great">Catherine</a> renamed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ural-river">Yaik</a> the Ural and the host the Ural <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossack</a> Host. It served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> in Central Asian campaigns. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-civil-war">Russian Civil War</a> the Ural Cossacks fought the Bolsheviks, and the host was destroyed in 1920.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/ural-cossack-host.jpg" alt="Ural Cossack Host" width="320" height="189"><figcaption>Image: Ilya Repin · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ilja_Jefimowitsch_Repin_-_Reply_of_the_Zaporozhian_Cossacks_-_Yorck.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1591 CE – 1920 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Uralsk</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Russian Orthodoxy, Old Believers</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Russian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/kazakhstan">Kazakhstan</a>, <a href="/countries/russia">Russia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Yaik Cossack Host, Yaik Cossacks</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1756&amp;focus=ural-cossack-host" aria-label="Ural Cossack Host on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5988 321 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Ural Cossack Host lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6308 577L5820 533M6308 577L6487 457"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5820 533h0M6487 457h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6308 577h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6308 577h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Uralsk. <a href="/atlas?year=1756&amp;focus=ural-cossack-host">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

